  "solution": "**Given**\n\nAverage sales in 2001, 2002, 2003 and 2004 is 1850\n\nAverage sales in 2002, 2003, 2004 and 2005 is 2125\n\nSales in 2005: 1200\n\n**Solution:**\n\nTotal sales from 2001 to 2004 = 1850 × 4 = 7400\n\n⇒ S(2001) + S(2002) + S(2003) + S(2004) = 7400 ----(01)\n\nTotal sales from 2002 to 2005 = 2125 × 4 = 8500\n\n⇒ S(2002) + S(2003) + S(2004) + S(2005) = 8500 ----(02)\n\nEquation(02) - Equation(01)\n\nS(2005) - S(2001) = 1100\n\n⇒ 1200 - S(2001) = 1100\n\n⇒ S(2001) = 1200 - 1100 = 100\n\n**∴ The sales in 2001 were 100.**",
